    "text": "14 minutes ago INDIANAPOLIS — SNAP funds earmarked for people in Indiana are delayed at least a week, the Indiana Family and Social Services Administration confirms to 13News. The Trump administration is using a contingency fund to partially fund SNAP across the country, but because of that, the state has to recalculate what each household receives. That takes time and intensifies uncertainties. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
